{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And YHWH shut him in.</b> He shielded it so they would not break it — the ark was surrounded by bears and lions that were killing among them. And the plain sense of Scripture: He closed it against him, against the waters. And so every בְּעַד in Scripture is a term of 'against': בְּעַד כָּל רֶחֶם (Genesis 20:18); בַּעֲדֵךְ וּבְעַד בָּנַיִךְ (II Kings 4); עוֹר בְּעַד עוֹר (Job 2); מָגֵן בַּעֲדִי (Psalms 3); הִתְפַּלֵּל בְּעַד עֲבָדֶיךָ (I Samuel 12) — against your servants."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:02.151733856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}